                        to release the path. Default is 0 (no timeout)␀use_lockfiles␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Enable or disable the usage of filesystem lockfiles for shared resources␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀
                        By default, mamba uses lockfiles on the filesystem to synchronize access to
                        shared resources for multiple mamba processes (such as the package cache).
                        However, some filesystems do not support file locking and locks do not always
                        make sense - like when on an HPC.  Default is true (use a lockfile␀compile_pyc␀␀␀␀Defines if PYC files will be compiled or not␀always_yes␀Output, Prompt and Flow Control␀Automatically answer yes on prompted questions␀auto_activate_base␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Automatically activate the base env␀␀␀␀␀
                        Automatically activate the base environment during shell
